.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

int session_handle(client_session_t *session, server_config_t *config);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Main session handler that processes client commands in a loop.
This is the entry point for all client interaction after connection
setup.
.PP
On entry, the function performs automatic protocol version detection by
calling \f[CR]protocol_detect_version()\f[R] to peek at the first byte
on the wire:
.IP \(bu 2
If the first byte is a v2 binary frame channel ID (0\(en5), delegates
immediately to \f[CR]json_session_handle()\f[R] with
\f[CR]PROTOCOL_V2\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
If the first byte is \f[CR]{\f[R] (0x7B), sets \f[CR]WIRE_NDJSON\f[R]
wire format and delegates to \f[CR]json_session_handle()\f[R] with
\f[CR]PROTOCOL_V2_NDJSON\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
Otherwise, falls through to the v1 text protocol handler.
.PP
In v1 mode, the function reads LF\-terminated lines via
\f[CR]protocol_read_line()\f[R], parses each into a command and argument
via \f[CR]protocol_parse_command()\f[R], and dispatches to the
appropriate handler:
.PP
