.TE
.PP
Commands requiring authentication return
\f[CR]ERR not authenticated\f[R] if the session has not yet completed a
successful \f[CR]AUTH\f[R] handshake.
Unknown commands return \f[CR]ERR unknown command: <cmd>\f[R].
.PP
The loop exits when \f[CR]QUIT\f[R] is received or
\f[CR]protocol_read_line()\f[R] returns an error (connection closed or
I/O error).
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]session\f[R] \(en Pointer to an initialized
\f[CR]client_session_t\f[R].
Must have been set up by \f[CR]session_init()\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]config\f[R] \(en Pointer to the server configuration.
Used to access the auth token for \f[CR]AUTH\f[R] validation and shell
initialization flags for \f[CR]init_bash_for_session()\f[R].
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \f[CR]0\f[R] on clean session exit (QUIT received or connection
closed).
Returns \f[CR]\-1\f[R] on protocol or I/O error.
.SH ERRORS
I/O errors on the client socket cause the loop to exit.
The specific errno is logged to stderr before returning.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]session_init\f[R](3), \f[CR]session_cleanup\f[R](3),
\f[CR]session_execute_command\f[R](3),
\f[CR]init_bash_for_session\f[R](3), \f[CR]json_session_handle\f[R](3),
\f[CR]protocol_detect_version\f[R](3)
.SH NOTES
The function uses \f[CR]session_wfd()\f[R] (an internal inline helper)
to determine the correct file descriptor for writing responses.
In socket mode, read and write use the same fd.
In stdio mode, \f[CR]fd\f[R] is stdin and \f[CR]write_fd\f[R] is stdout.
.PP
Protocol version detection is performed only once, on the first byte.
Once v1 is selected, the session remains in v1 mode for its lifetime.
.PP
Shell state (variables, functions, aliases, working directory, traps)
persists across EVAL commands within a single session because command
execution happens in\-process via \f[CR]parse_and_execute()\f[R].
